{
  "note": "§6: the succession-graph version is a **retry**, not a terminal refusal — the relation moved, so the decision is made again rather than reported against a graph that no longer exists. The retry then finds the slot occupied and the denial says so, which is the honest answer: this admission lost a race it can name, not an unexplained `contended`.",
  "kind": "core.r5e.io/v1/Succession",
  "interleave": {
    "kind": "core.r5e.io/v1/Succession",
